- [x] Isolated agent worktrees start from upstream origin/main, not local main #tooling #where(.git/config) #added(2026-11-11) #done(2026-11-12)
	> Local main tracks origin/main (the upstream fork), and an Agent with worktree
	> isolation is cut at origin/main (722c7b4, upstream v1.4) instead of local main; every
	> agent prompt has to start with 'git checkout -B <branch> main'. Setting main's
	> upstream to fork/main does not help (probed 2026-11-11: a worktree agent still
	> started at 722c7b4; origin/HEAD -> origin/main). Likely fix: rename the remotes so
	> origin is the fork (sX11/my-band) and upstream is matheusdanoite/my-band. Cost: every
	> upstream comparison (git show origin/main:..., the port workflow) and gh's default
	> repo change names.
